Sacco in Greek means, The girl with small bladder :)P..</center><br><br></span><span class="normal"><br>        </span></p>      </td>  </tr>  <tr background="barre1.jpg">     <td background="barre1.jpg">&nbsp;</td>    <td background="barre1.jpg"class="auteur">Euromancer</td>  </tr>  <tr><td colspan="2"><br></td></tr>    <td width="560" background="barre.jpg"><span class="GTitre">big smile</span><br> </td>    <td width="140" background="barre.jpg" class="date"><div align="right">16/09/2003</div></td>  </tr>  <tr>     <td bgcolor="#2F2828" colspan="2"><p><br>        <span class="normal">As you have noticed the <b>MtS</b> web site have under gone a redesign and revamp.  The new design has been under taken by <b>Saradoc</b> better know to his friends as Doc, better know to people who think they are funny as A$$ling ><.<br />
<br><br />
Anyway we here at <b>MtS</b> would like to say a BIG thank you to saradoc for his web design skills (or lack of them if the site goes down, regardless if it is his fault of not >< muhahaha) and keep up the good work with the further implementation of the additional models that will be added over the next week or so, which will add great functionality to our site and make it the best in the land.<br />
<br><br />
I would like to ask all <b>MtS</b> members to fill in your roster profile, details of which are on the private section of the web site making sure you get your flag information filled in ASAP otherwise this Gnomer is going to be sending Sacco round to sort you out and maybe Bashina (PMT can be a bitch).<br />
</span><span class="normal"><br>        </span></p>      </td>  </tr>  <tr background="barre1.jpg">     <td background="barre1.jpg">&nbsp;</td>    <td background="barre1.jpg"class="auteur">Euromancer</td>  </tr>  <tr><td colspan="2"><br></td></tr>    <td width="560" background="barre.jpg"><span class="GTitre">EQ > RL</span><br> </td>    <td width="140" background="barre.jpg" class="date"><div align="right">12/09/2003</div></td>  </tr>  <tr>     <td bgcolor="#2F2828" colspan="2"><p><br>        <span class="normal">Itís been a bit of a slow old week and no new encounters, but none the less MtS have been busy as usual. We are still taking recruits, although the specification has been raised to reflect the guild's advancement and the need's to class balance. It is still possible to be a MtS member, but please be aware we require a higher class of player. This is inclusive of the normal high personal attributes we look for in a recruit. Even if your specific class is flagged as not needed at the minute post in the recruitment forum and add at the bottom why you would be an assett to MtS.<br />
So what have we been doing?<br />
Well of late itís been a recruitment extravaganza, well maybe not that grand but you get the picture. So its back to revisit PoP flag mobs to get the guild up to date and all singing from the same hymn sheet. Not in any specific order by the way.<br />
<br />
1. Vallon Zek<br />
2. Tallon Zek<br />
3. Saryrn<br />
4. Grummus<br />
5. HoH Trails<br />
6. Mitherial Marr<br />
7. Manaetic Behmoth<br />
8. PoN Hedge<br />
9. Terris Thule<br />
10. CrushBone (Die hard raiders ><..)<br />
<br />
Probly some others but I forget them if there is. The guild is on the verge of breaking into Elemental Planes and these are exciting times of new challenges and of even better ways to wipe :). Seen one Grave Yard you seen em all.<br />
<br />
== You don't have to be on Drugs in MtS but having a puff of the Bong helps ==<br />
<br />
Here MtS we do not take ourselves too serious otherwise we wouldnít let Dorfs join muhahaha. Keeping in that spirit I would like to present Aazeroth.<br />
<br />
<CENTER><IMG src="http://ion.dc.luth.se/pics/aaz1.jpeg"><BR>I have the POWER 0==[]=== HE-MAN ===><BR><br />
<CENTER><IMG src="http://ion.dc.luth.se/pics/aaz2.jpeg"><BR>What yah mean I left the WebCam on...<BR><br />
<IMG src="http://ion.dc.luth.se/pics/aaz3.jpeg"><BR></CENTER></span><span class="normal"><br>        </span></p>      </td>  </tr>  <tr background="barre1.jpg">     <td background="barre1.jpg">&nbsp;</td>    <td background="barre1.jpg"class="auteur">Euromancer</td>  </tr>  <tr><td colspan="2"><br></td></tr>    <td width="560" background="barre.jpg"><span class="GTitre">A little something, something.</span><br> </td>    <td width="140" background="barre.jpg" class="date"><div align="right">24/08/2003</div></td>  </tr>  <tr>     <td bgcolor="#2F2828" colspan="2"><p><br>        <span class="normal">Time once more for the VT trail and with two previous VTís under the preverbal belt we head in again with full knowledge of what the night will hold. Thatís right the mammoth amount of mobs to clear, the unknown amount of wipe recovering and the best of all, the loot. Hoping for none of the first two and a lot of the last option. It took a full night but look what we came away with /big grin.<BR><BR><B>.: Kaas Thox Xi Ans Dyek :.</B><BR><A href="http://ion.dc.luth.se/dkp/plugins/stats/itemshot.php?s=&i=28897">Gauntlets of Dark Embers</A> ñ <B>Lupinus</B><BR><A href="http://ion.dc.luth.se/dkp/plugins/stats/itemshot.php?s=&i=28903">Orb of Evasion</A> ñ <B>Buzzi</B><BR><BR><B>.: Diabo Xi Va :.</B><BR><A href="http://ion.dc.luth.se/dkp/plugins/stats/itemshot.php?s=&i=28980">Rune of Judgement</A> ñ <B>Lluuvil</B><BR><A href="http://ion.dc.luth.se/dkp/plugins/stats/itemshot.php?s=&i=28980">Staff of Lost Rituals</A> ñ <B>Tassador</B><BR><A href="http://ion.dc.luth.se/dkp/plugins/stats/itemshot.php?s=&i=28981">Grimoire of Enchantment</A> ñ <B>Opalinae</B><BR><BR><B>.: Diabo Xi Xin Thall :.</B><BR><A href="http://ion.dc.luth.se/dkp/plugins/stats/itemshot.php?s=&i=28910">Robe of Luring Shadows</A> ñ <B>Niclas</B><BR><A href="http://ion.dc.luth.se/dkp/plugins/stats/itemshot.php?s=&i=28914">Ring of the Crimson Bull</A> ñ <B>Buzzi & Pamilai</B><BR><BR><B>.: Thall Va Kelun :.</B><BR><A href="http://ion.dc.luth.se/dkp/plugins/stats/itemshot.php?s=&i=28964">Cloak of Frozen Flames</A> ñ <B>Crostmost</B><BR><A href="http://ion.dc.luth.se/dkp/plugins/stats/itemshot.php?s=&i=28967">Gloves of Warding</A> ñ <B>Boladas</B><BR><A href="http://ion.dc.luth.se/dkp/plugins/stats/itemshot.php?s=&i=28965">Leggings of Fiery Might</A> ñ <B>Rigo</B><BR><br />
<CENTER><IMG src="http://ion.dc.luth.se/pics/Yogaised.jpg"><BR>Thats gonna hurt in the morning.</CENTER><BR><BR><B>.: Thall Xundraux Diabo :.</B><BR><A href="http://ion.dc.luth.se/dkp/plugins/stats/itemshot.php?s=&i=28939">Hoop of Chaos</A> ñ <B>Buzzi</B><BR><A href="http://ion.dc.luth.se/dkp/plugins/stats/itemshot.php?s=&i=28940">Shadow Pearl Earring</A> ñ <B>Pouppee</B><BR><A href="http://ion.dc.luth.se/dkp/plugins/stats/itemshot.php?s=&i=28936">Great Cloak of Shadows</A> ñ <B>Mordekay</B><BR><BR><B>.: Va Xi Aten Ha Ra :.</B><BR><A href="http://ion.dc.luth.se/dkp/plugins/stats/itemshot.php?s=&i=28943">Cloudy Mark</A> ñ <B>Shaggat</B><BR><A href="http://ion.dc.luth.se/dkp/plugins/stats/itemshot.php?s=&i=28948">Eye of Darkness</A> ñ <B>Yoshboy</B><BR><A href="http://ion.dc.luth.se/dkp/plugins/stats/itemshot.php?s=&i=28945">Earring of Battle</A> ñ <B>Mordekay</B><BR><br />
